/-!
# The whole module and marked parabolic in 13.5.21

The common source deductions prove relative normality of K, ambient and
quotient commutator generation, and U_H=[Q_H,K]. The marked stabilizer
is defined on the original faithful binary action. Its model index bound
implies the exact L₁*T* equality and two-residual marking.

This module retains assembly of the natural central quotient and all three
concrete marked-parabolic cases. Those conclusions and the L₁-generation
needed for 13.5.14 remain unfinished; no whole-module irreducibility or
splitting is asserted.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
Lemma 13.5.21, printed pp.923–924 (PDF pp.940–941).
-/
